(I)--the members of the fourth वर्ण;
1: भा. I. १३. १५; II. 1. ३७; 7. ३८ and ४६; VII. ११. २४.
their duty was service;
2: Ib. VIII. 5. ४१; XI. १७. १९.
not fit for the study of the Vedas;
3: Ib. X. २४. २०; ३८. 4.
invited for the राजसूय of युधिष्टिर;
4: Ib. X. ७४. ११.
kings of Kali age, especially after Puramjaya;
5: Ib. XI. 4. २२; 5. 4; १२. 4; २७. 4; XII. 1. 8 and ३८; 2. ३५.
receive gifts, become ascetics and expound dharma from high places in Kali;
6: Ib. XII. 3. ३८.
duty was dharma परिचार yajn5a; take to ब्राह्मण dharma in Kali yuga; not fit for panktibhojanam. For the sake of 1,००० S4u1dras, one ब्राह्- मण may be killed; creation of: पृषध्र born a शूद्र by cow-slaughter;
7: Br. II. २९. ५५; ३१. ३९४ and ३६७; III. १०. ९६; ११. ८७; १५. ४४; ६८. ६७; IV. 6. ४३.
meditate on देवी's १०८ names; perform श्राद्- dha with no mantras;
8: M. 4. २८; १२. २५; १३. ६३; १७. ६४, ७०-71.
observe a month's pollution for father's death; ययाति's benevolence to; शूद्र kings rooted out by Kalki;
9: Ib. १८. 3; ३४. 5; ४७. २५०. ५०. ७५; १४४. ३९-54.
may observe रोहिणिचन्द्र s4ayanam and अन्गारक vratam.
१०: Ib. ५७. 6; ७२. २०-1; ११४. १२; २१७. 2.

(II)--created out of the feet of the Lord;
1: Vi. I. 6. 6.
गान्- dharvam स्थानम्;
2: Ib. I. 6. ३५.
duties of;
3: Ib. III. 8. ३३-4.
as kings from the time of Ma- हापद्म;
4: Ib. IV. २४. २१ and ६८.
take to asceticism and become followers of here- tical sects; no regard for age, learning and family;
5: वा. ५८. ४०-41; Vi. VI. 1. ३७.
fortunate, because they do not have to undergo the ordeals of perform- ing rituals and ceremonials incumbent on the twice born castes; not fettered by restrictions of any sort.
6: Ib. VI. 2. २३. 4.

(I)--a weapon of कृष्ण, known as Cakra;
1: भा. I. 8. १३; III. १९. २२; VIII. 4. १९.
reached कृष्ण when मथुरा was besieged by जरासन्ध, and was used to kill शतधन्वा;
2: Ib. X. ५० 11[2]; ५७. २१.
sent to the sun and moon to ward off राहु's attack;
3: Ib. V. २४. 3.
presented to अम्बरीष; fell upon दुर्वास when he raised a spirit to attack अम्बरीष who begged to spare the sage and the Cakra did so;
4: Ib. IX. 4. २८ & ४८; ५२. ११ & १२; XI. २७. २७; XII. ११. १४; Br. III. 5. २८. ४०. ६६.
a weapon of Hari, at काशी.
5: M. V. २९. १७; ३०. ६७; ३३. ३५; ३४. ३७.
